// Translations of CybBee's own editorial guides. Original source links stay on the guide.
const article=(intro,sections,scenarios,checklist,faq)=>({intro,sections:sections.map(([title,text])=>({title,text})),scenarios,checklist,faq,localizedFull:true,localizedSummary:false});
export const fullGuideLocales={en:{
winter:article('Winter preparation starts well before frost. Prepare the colony, then observe it in winter with as little disturbance as possible. This guide supports decisions; food requirements and insulation depend on your climate.',[
 ['Before cold weather','Gather the latest complete colony record: strength, queen and brood observations, accessible stores, Varroa monitoring and actions taken. List unanswered questions separately. Winter-bee preparation and mite management require attention during the active season.'],
 ['Winter observation','Start with external signs: roof condition, entrance access, hive stability and changes after wind or snow. Weight measurements are useful when interpreted for the hive construction. One observation does not establish either colony health or colony loss.']
],[['Hive appears much lighter','Record how weight was assessed. Compare previous records and discuss stores assessment with a local mentor. Do not import a feeding allowance from another climate.'],['An internal inspection is needed','Identify the specific question first. Choose appropriate conditions and a method; do not open the nest daily just to complete an app entry.']],['Date and weather','Stores-assessment method','External changes and photographs','Next check with a clear purpose'],[['Must I open the hive every day?','No. A daily entry may record external observations rather than nest inspection.'],['Does the winter theme mean the colony should be wintering?','No. The theme follows month and hemisphere; husbandry decisions follow local conditions.']]),
swarm:article('Swarming is colony reproduction and also a management concern. Distinguish swarm prevention in your hive from collecting an already departed swarm: their circumstances and risks differ.',[
 ['What to record','Record colony strength, available space and queen-cell condition. Describe what was actually seen rather than simply predicting swarming. An empty queen cup and a developing queen cell are different observations. Photographs and an experienced mentor can help interpret them.'],
 ['If a swarm has been found','Record location and access without bringing unprotected people close. Prepare a hive and separate follow-up observation. The colony’s origin and health are unknown, so combining it with another colony should not be an automatic next step.']
],[['Cluster on a low accessible branch','Assess your skills and whether an experienced beekeeper can help. Choose a collection plan for the situation rather than a universal recipe.'],['Bees near wires, high up or inside a wall','Do not climb or dismantle structures yourself. Contact specialists experienced in these situations.']],['Discovery date','Location and safe access','Known or unknown origin','Separate hive and follow-up plan'],[['Can one queen cell establish swarming?','Assess brood, queen observations and colony history. Colonies raise queens for different reasons.'],['What should be recorded after settlement?','Colony condition, follow-up observations and the chosen inspection plan.']]),
queen:article('Introducing a queen is a process, not simply opening a cage. Establish colony condition and the protocol appropriate to this particular queen. If uncertain, clarify the situation before risking the queen.',[
 ['Before introduction','Record the replacement reason, queen origin, receipt date and supplier information. Separately record whether the old queen’s absence is established, and what is known about eggs and queen cells. Virgin, mated and instrumentally inseminated queens may require different approaches.'],
 ['Check the outcome','Follow the supplier’s instructions and selected introduction protocol. Plan observations of acceptance and confirmation of egg laying. Release alone does not establish acceptance. Keep introduction and confirmed-result dates separate.']
],[['Unsure whether the colony is queenless','Do not replace blindly. Clarify the signs and ask an experienced mentor.'],['Queen released but outcome unknown','Record that confirmation is pending. Schedule the next inspection according to the protocol rather than a daily notification.']],['Reason and colony condition','Queen type, source and year','Supplier protocol','Introduction date and separate outcome date'],[['Does one release interval suit every queen?','No. Do not reuse someone else’s timing without checking circumstances.'],['Can AI decide when to release her?','AI can help formulate questions, but cannot inspect your colony or confirm acceptance.']]),
varroa:article('Varroa management follows measurement, selection of a measure and follow-up. A treatment record is useful, but measurements help assess what happened afterwards.',[
 ['Comparable observations','Record the method, sample size and mite count. Interpret results with the method and brood condition in mind. Zero mites in one sample do not prove absence. Decision thresholds depend on local conditions; one worldwide number is inappropriate.'],
 ['Selecting measures','Combine monitoring with suitable colony-management practices. Check product registration, temperature, brood and honey-super restrictions. Consult the current product label, not only the active ingredient’s name.']
],[['Readings deteriorate','Check that samples are comparable and review the chosen plan. Discuss changes with a local specialist.'],['Treatment completed','Schedule further monitoring according to the protocol. Do not mark the colony mite-free without checking.']],['Method and sample size','Mite count and colony condition','Product, label and date','Follow-up result'],[['Does a negative sample mean no Varroa?','No. Sampling represents only part of the situation, especially when brood is present.'],['Should every hive have one identical plan?','Colony conditions can differ. Keep records for each hive.']]),
oxalic:article('The name oxalic acid alone does not establish a suitable product, dose or schedule. Record the conditions and current label first. CybBee does not calculate mixtures or prescribe repeat treatments.',[
 ['Conditions determine the next step','Record country, registered product name and method. Check restrictions concerning brood, honey supers, temperature and colony condition. A US or UK product label does not authorize its use in another country.'],
 ['Preparation and records','Follow label requirements for equipment, operator protection and application. Record the monitoring result supporting the decision beforehand. Afterwards, record actual date, product and planned efficacy check. Keep the action and its outcome separate.']
],[['No current registered-product label','Do not construct a treatment protocol from chat advice. Find the current document and establish its applicability.'],['Brood or honey supers are present','Check the restrictions for your exact product and method. Permission for another product cannot be substituted.']],['Country and product','HTTPS link to current label','Method and colony conditions','Equipment and protection requirements','Actual application and follow-up'],[['Why is there no universal dose?','Products, methods and registrations differ. An error can harm the colony or operator.'],['When should treatment be repeated?','Only as allowed by the current label and monitoring plan, not the app’s general calendar.']]),
'first-visit':article('A useful inspection answers specific questions and ends with a clear record. Do not attempt every possible job in one visit. Prepare equipment, protection and an observation list.',[['Writing a useful record','Instead of “everything is fine”, state which signs were assessed. If uncertain, write “queen not found during this inspection” rather than “no queen”. This helps explain later how decisions were made.']],[['A sign cannot be assessed confidently','Record uncertainty and a question for a mentor. Do not diagnose from one photograph.']],['Visit purpose','Hive, date and conditions','Facts separated from assumptions','Next task'],[['Must every field be completed?','No. An honest incomplete entry is better than invented measurements.']]),
spring:article('Spring is not a fixed apiary date. Colonies and plants respond to local conditions. Use the seasonal theme to organize questions, rather than as an instruction to open every hive.',[['Linking observations to the calendar','Create tasks prompted by observations, such as reassessing stores or clarifying queen status. CybBee stores your dates; do not transfer Northern Hemisphere timing to the south without considering local seasons.']],[['The calendar says spring but conditions are unsuitable','Do not perform an internal inspection just to tick a box. Assess what can be observed externally.']],['Winter outcome','Stores and brood','Local conditions','First flowering observations'],[['Will timing from a neighbouring region apply?','Compare climate, elevation and local observations. Applicability is not guaranteed.']]),
summer:article('A summer journal separates expectations from results. A flowering meadow, flight activity and increased stores are related but distinct observations. Describe each separately.',[['Recording the honey flow','Record date, weather, visible changes and measurement method. Without scales, do not invent precise kilograms from an impression. Comparable records help identify recurring conditions after the season.']],[['A plant is flowering but no result is apparent','Record the observation without asserting a guaranteed honey flow. Clarify plant identity and conditions.']],['Plant and location','Date and weather','Method of assessing change','Next job'],[['Can a map promise a harvest?','No. A map shows locations and records, not a guaranteed yield.']]),
autumn:article('The season review lists confirmed outcomes and unanswered questions for each colony. It makes winter preparation manageable and preserves important observations.',[['Reviewing the season','Record which decisions helped, which observations were incomplete and what was missing. Export a backup and, with consent, exchange the journal with your account. Consistent hive names and observation methods help comparisons across years.']],[['Information is missing for a colony','Create a clarification task. Do not fill gaps with assumptions to make a report look complete.']],['Health review','Stores assessment','Winter plan','Downloaded backup'],[['Does every colony need the same amount of feed?','Requirements depend on climate, hive construction and condition. Consult local guidance.']]),
feeding:article('Feeding should address an identified colony need rather than become an automatic procedure for every hive. First assess whether food is needed and accessible to the bees.',[['Feed origin','Do not move honey combs of unknown origin or from suspect colonies without a health assessment. Record their source and why they are used. Suitable feed and safety matter more than using a convenient leftover.']],[['Need is not established','Clarify stores assessment. Do not feed simply because the app displays a winter theme.']],['Reason and assessment method','Feed source','Date and selected method','Follow-up'],[['Can I import a Minnesota allowance?','Not automatically. Published allowances refer to a particular climate and husbandry system.']]),
journal:article('CybBee connects observations, decisions and the next job. A private journal is separate from the community and map, which have their own publication controls.',[['Where data is kept','The journal has IndexedDB storage and a browser copy. Cloud exchange is account-bound and merges separate records. Conflicting versions require your choice. Optional automatic exchange runs only while the app is open and visible, after separate consent. Photos have their own transfer permission; books and sensor readings need separate exports. Clearing site data removes local copies. A downloaded backup is separate from browser storage.']],[['Using two devices','Exchange changes before and after editing. If the same record differs, inspect both versions. Do not force an overwrite; cancel if uncertain and export a backup.'],['Sharing an observation','Create a separate community entry. Review its text and confirm public publication; journal sync does not publish it.']],['Recognizable hive names','Facts separated from opinions','Downloaded backup','Confirmed save and exchange status'],[['Does signing in mean everything was backed up?','No. Check journal and photo transfer status separately. Optional automatic exchange does not run when the app is closed.']]),
'community-guide':article('A useful post lets another beekeeper understand the observation’s circumstances. Separate a description of your apiary from advice claimed to apply everywhere.',[['A useful structure','General region and season → colony condition → action → observed result → question. This provides context without disclosing your apiary’s precise address.']],[['A post contains questionable advice','Ask for a source. Report inappropriate content rather than trying a dangerous procedure to test it.']],['Context','Observed facts','Source for recommendations','Privacy review'],[['Is the public chat encrypted like a private conversation?','No. It is a public feed. Do not post secrets or personal information.']]),
honey:article('Honey work connects colony condition, careful food handling and records. A flowering field does not guarantee yield. Base harvesting decisions on actual stores and local requirements.',[['Batch traceability','Use the honey ledger to record hive, date, measured mass, batch label and floral-source note. These notes do not certify botanical origin. Record containers, storage and subsequent actions in the journal. Dedicated stock movements and label production are not implemented. Before selling, check local premises, labelling and record requirements.']],[['Planning to sell honey','Check local food requirements first. Guidance from another country does not replace your region’s rules.'],['A batch has unclear origin','Clarify the records before blending batches. Keep an honest unknown-source note.']],['Batch date and source','Product history and restrictions','Measured mass','Containers and storage','Local sale requirements'],[['Can a map establish lime honey?','No. A map and flowering observations do not establish the batch’s botanical origin.'],['Does the app manage warehouse stock?','No. The ledger records harvests and expenses; full stock movements are not implemented.']])
}};
Object.assign(fullGuideLocales,{
zh:{winter:article('越冬准备应在霜冻前很久开始。养蜂人先做好蜂群准备，冬季再尽量少打扰地观察。本指南帮助梳理决策；饲料数量与保温方式须按当地气候确定。',[
 ['寒冷到来之前','整理蜂群最近一次完整记录：群势、蜂王与育虫情况、可取用储粮、瓦螨监测结果和已采取措施。另列尚未弄清的问题。越冬蜂培育与控螨需要在活跃季节就得到关注。'],
 ['冬季观察','先从外部观察：箱盖、巢门是否畅通、蜂箱稳固性以及风雪后的变化。称重只有结合蜂箱结构才有意义。一次观察既不能证明蜂群健康，也不能证明蜂群死亡。']
],[['蜂箱似乎明显变轻','记录如何评估重量，与旧记录比较，并向当地导师咨询储粮评估。不要照搬其他气候区的饲喂量。'],['需要内部检查','先明确具体问题，再选择合适条件和方法。不要为填写应用记录而每天开箱。']],['日期与天气','储粮评估方法','外部变化与照片','下一次检查的明确目的'],[['必须每天开箱吗？','不必。每日记录可以是外部观察，而不是拆检蜂巢。'],['冬季主题表示蜂群应该越冬吗？','不是。界面主题按月份与半球变化，养蜂决策应依据当地条件。']])},
hi:{winter:article('सर्दियों की तैयारी पाला पड़ने से बहुत पहले शुरू होती है। पहले कॉलोनी तैयार करें, फिर सर्दियों में कम से कम व्यवधान के साथ निरीक्षण करें। यह मार्गदर्शिका निर्णय समझने में मदद करती है; आहार और इन्सुलेशन अपनी जलवायु के अनुसार चुनें।',[
 ['ठंड आने से पहले','कॉलोनी का नवीनतम पूरा रिकॉर्ड जुटाएँ: शक्ति, रानी और ब्रूड के अवलोकन, सुलभ भंडार, Varroa निगरानी तथा किए गए उपाय। अनुत्तरित प्रश्न अलग लिखें। शीतकालीन मधुमक्खियों की तैयारी और माइट नियंत्रण पर सक्रिय मौसम में ही ध्यान चाहिए।'],
 ['सर्दियों में अवलोकन','बाहरी संकेतों से शुरू करें: छत, प्रवेश द्वार, छत्ते की स्थिरता और हवा या बर्फ के बाद बदलाव। वजन का अर्थ छत्ते की बनावट के संदर्भ में समझें। एक अवलोकन से कॉलोनी का स्वस्थ होना या नष्ट होना सिद्ध नहीं होता।']
],[['छत्ता पहले से काफी हल्का लगता है','वजन आँकने की विधि लिखें। पिछले रिकॉर्ड से तुलना करें और स्थानीय मार्गदर्शक से भंडार आकलन पर चर्चा करें। दूसरी जलवायु का आहार मानक न अपनाएँ।'],['अंदर जाँच जरूरी है','पहले स्पष्ट प्रश्न तय करें। उचित परिस्थितियाँ और विधि चुनें; ऐप में निशान लगाने के लिए रोज़ छत्ता न खोलें।']],['तारीख और मौसम','भंडार आकलन की विधि','बाहरी बदलाव और फ़ोटो','अगली जाँच का स्पष्ट उद्देश्य'],[['क्या हर दिन छत्ता खोलना चाहिए?','नहीं। दैनिक प्रविष्टि बाहरी अवलोकन की हो सकती है, ब्रूड घोंसले की जाँच की नहीं।'],['क्या शीतकालीन थीम का अर्थ है कि कॉलोनी को अब सर्दी की अवस्था में होना चाहिए?','नहीं। थीम महीना और गोलार्ध देखकर बदलती है; निर्णय स्थानीय परिस्थितियों से लें।']])},
es:{winter:article('La preparación invernal empieza mucho antes de las heladas. Prepare la colonia y obsérvela en invierno con la menor perturbación posible. Esta guía ayuda a decidir; ajuste alimento y aislamiento a su clima.',[
 ['Antes del frío','Reúna el último registro completo: fuerza, observaciones de reina y cría, reservas accesibles, control de Varroa y medidas realizadas. Anote aparte las preguntas pendientes. La preparación de abejas de invierno y el control del ácaro requieren atención durante la temporada activa.'],
 ['Observación invernal','Empiece por signos externos: techo, acceso a la piquera, estabilidad y cambios tras viento o nieve. Interprete el peso según la construcción de la colmena. Una observación no demuestra bienestar ni pérdida de la colonia.']
],[['La colmena parece mucho más ligera','Anote cómo evaluó el peso. Compare registros previos y consulte las reservas con un mentor local. No copie cantidades de alimentación de otro clima.'],['Hace falta una inspección interior','Defina primero una pregunta concreta. Elija condiciones y método adecuados; no abra el nido a diario para marcar una casilla.']],['Fecha y tiempo','Método de evaluación de reservas','Cambios externos y fotografías','Próxima revisión con un objetivo claro'],[['¿Debo abrir la colmena cada día?','No. Una entrada diaria puede describir observaciones externas sin desmontar el nido.'],['¿La temática invernal indica que la colonia debe invernar?','No. La apariencia sigue el mes y hemisferio; las decisiones siguen las condiciones locales.']])},
ar:{winter:article('يبدأ الاستعداد للشتاء قبل الصقيع بوقت طويل. جهّز الطائفة ثم راقبها شتاءً بأقل إزعاج ممكن. يساعد هذا الدليل في اتخاذ القرار؛ حدّد كمية الغذاء والعزل وفق مناخ منطقتك.',[
 ['قبل البرد','اجمع أحدث سجل كامل: قوة الطائفة وملاحظات الملكة والحضنة والمخزون المتاح ونتائج رصد الفاروا والإجراءات المنفذة. دوّن الأسئلة غير المحسومة منفصلة. إعداد نحل الشتاء ومكافحة الفاروا يحتاجان إلى اهتمام أثناء الموسم النشط.'],
 ['المراقبة شتاءً','ابدأ بالعلامات الخارجية: السقف ومدخل الخلية وثباتها والتغيرات بعد الرياح أو الثلج. فسّر الوزن بحسب تركيب الخلية. لا تثبت ملاحظة واحدة سلامة الطائفة أو فقدانها.']
],[['تبدو الخلية أخف كثيراً','سجّل طريقة تقدير الوزن، وقارن السجلات السابقة، واستشر مرشداً محلياً بشأن المخزون. لا تنقل كمية تغذية من مناخ آخر.'],['تحتاج إلى فحص داخلي','حدّد السؤال أولاً ثم اختر ظروفاً وطريقة مناسبتين. لا تفتح العش يومياً لمجرد تسجيل علامة في التطبيق.']],['التاريخ والطقس','طريقة تقدير المخزون','التغيرات الخارجية والصور','هدف واضح للفحص التالي'],[['هل يجب فتح الخلية يومياً؟','لا. قد يكون السجل اليومي وصفاً لمراقبة خارجية دون تفكيك العش.'],['هل يعني مظهر الشتاء أن على الطائفة الدخول في الشتاء؟','لا. يتبع المظهر الشهر ونصف الكرة؛ وتتبع القرارات الظروف المحلية.']])},
pt:{winter:article('A preparação para o inverno começa muito antes das geadas. Prepare a colônia e observe-a no inverno com a menor perturbação possível. Este guia orienta decisões; ajuste alimento e isolamento ao clima local.',[
 ['Antes do frio','Reúna o registro completo mais recente: força, observações da rainha e da cria, reservas acessíveis, monitoramento de Varroa e medidas tomadas. Liste separadamente as dúvidas. Preparar abelhas de inverno e controlar ácaros exige atenção ainda na estação ativa.'],
 ['Observação no inverno','Comece pelos sinais externos: cobertura, acesso ao alvado, estabilidade e mudanças após vento ou neve. Interprete o peso considerando a construção da colmeia. Uma observação não comprova saúde nem perda da colônia.']
],[['A colmeia parece muito mais leve','Registre como avaliou o peso. Compare registros anteriores e discuta as reservas com um orientador local. Não copie uma quantidade de alimentação de outro clima.'],['É necessária inspeção interna','Defina primeiro uma pergunta específica. Escolha condições e método adequados; não abra o ninho diariamente para marcar uma tarefa.']],['Data e tempo','Método de avaliação das reservas','Mudanças externas e fotos','Objetivo claro da próxima verificação'],[['É preciso abrir a colmeia diariamente?','Não. Um registro diário pode descrever observação externa, sem desmontar o ninho.'],['O tema de inverno significa que a colônia deve estar em invernada?','Não. O tema segue mês e hemisfério; decisões seguem as condições locais.']])},
bn:{winter:article('তুষারপাতের অনেক আগেই শীতের প্রস্তুতি শুরু হয়। আগে কলোনি প্রস্তুত করুন, পরে শীতে যত কম বিরক্ত করে সম্ভব পর্যবেক্ষণ করুন। এই নির্দেশিকা সিদ্ধান্ত সাজাতে সাহায্য করে; খাবারের পরিমাণ ও নিরোধক নিজের জলবায়ু অনুযায়ী ঠিক করুন।',[
 ['ঠান্ডার আগে','কলোনির সর্বশেষ পূর্ণ রেকর্ড সংগ্রহ করুন: শক্তি, রানি ও ব্রুডের পর্যবেক্ষণ, ব্যবহারযোগ্য খাদ্যভান্ডার, Varroa পর্যবেক্ষণ ও নেওয়া ব্যবস্থা। অমীমাংসিত প্রশ্ন আলাদা লিখুন। শীতের মৌমাছি তৈরি ও মাইট নিয়ন্ত্রণে সক্রিয় মৌসুমেই মনোযোগ দরকার।'],
 ['শীতের পর্যবেক্ষণ','বাইরের লক্ষণ দিয়ে শুরু করুন: ছাদ, প্রবেশপথ, বাক্সের স্থায়িত্ব এবং বাতাস বা তুষারের পরের পরিবর্তন। বাক্সের গঠন বুঝে ওজন ব্যাখ্যা করুন। একবারের পর্যবেক্ষণে কলোনির সুস্থতা বা মৃত্যু প্রমাণ হয় না।']
],[['বাক্স আগের চেয়ে অনেক হালকা মনে হচ্ছে','কীভাবে ওজন আন্দাজ করেছেন লিখুন। পুরোনো রেকর্ডের সঙ্গে তুলনা করে স্থানীয় অভিজ্ঞ ব্যক্তির সঙ্গে খাদ্যভান্ডার নিয়ে আলোচনা করুন। অন্য জলবায়ুর খাদ্যের পরিমাণ নকল করবেন না।'],['ভেতরে পরীক্ষা দরকার','আগে নির্দিষ্ট প্রশ্ন ঠিক করুন। উপযুক্ত পরিস্থিতি ও পদ্ধতি বেছে নিন; অ্যাপে টিক দেওয়ার জন্য রোজ বাসা খুলবেন না।']],['তারিখ ও আবহাওয়া','খাদ্যভান্ডার মূল্যায়নের পদ্ধতি','বাইরের পরিবর্তন ও ছবি','পরের পরীক্ষার স্পষ্ট উদ্দেশ্য'],[['প্রতিদিন কি বাক্স খোলা দরকার?','না। দৈনিক নথি বাইরের পর্যবেক্ষণের হতে পারে, বাসা খুলে দেখার নয়।'],['শীতের থিম কি কলোনিকে শীতযাপন শুরু করতে বলে?','না। থিম মাস ও গোলার্ধ অনুসরণ করে; সিদ্ধান্ত নির্ভর করে স্থানীয় পরিস্থিতির ওপর।']])},
fr:{winter:article('La préparation hivernale commence bien avant les gelées. Préparez la colonie, puis observez-la en hiver en la dérangeant le moins possible. Ce guide aide à décider ; adaptez provisions et isolation à votre climat.',[
 ['Avant le froid','Rassemblez le dernier relevé complet : force, observations de reine et de couvain, réserves accessibles, suivi de Varroa et mesures prises. Notez séparément les questions sans réponse. La préparation des abeilles d’hiver et la gestion des acariens demandent une attention dès la saison active.'],
 ['Observation en hiver','Commencez par l’extérieur : toit, accès à l’entrée, stabilité et changements après vent ou neige. Interprétez le poids selon la construction de la ruche. Une observation ne prouve ni la bonne santé ni la perte d’une colonie.']
],[['La ruche semble bien plus légère','Notez la méthode d’évaluation du poids. Comparez les anciens relevés et discutez des réserves avec un mentor local. Ne transposez pas une ration d’un autre climat.'],['Une inspection interne est nécessaire','Définissez d’abord une question précise. Choisissez des conditions et une méthode adaptées ; n’ouvrez pas le nid chaque jour pour cocher une case.']],['Date et météo','Méthode d’évaluation des réserves','Changements extérieurs et photos','Objectif clair de la prochaine vérification'],[['Faut-il ouvrir la ruche tous les jours ?','Non. Un relevé quotidien peut décrire une observation extérieure sans démontage du nid.'],['Le thème hivernal impose-t-il l’hivernage ?','Non. Le thème suit le mois et l’hémisphère ; les décisions suivent les conditions locales.']])},
de:{winter:article('Die Wintervorbereitung beginnt lange vor dem Frost. Bereiten Sie das Volk vor und beobachten Sie es im Winter möglichst störungsarm. Diese Anleitung unterstützt Entscheidungen; Futterbedarf und Dämmung richten sich nach Ihrem Klima.',[
 ['Vor der Kälte','Sammeln Sie die letzte vollständige Aufzeichnung: Volksstärke, Königinnen- und Brutbeobachtungen, erreichbare Vorräte, Varroa-Monitoring und durchgeführte Maßnahmen. Halten Sie offene Fragen getrennt fest. Winterbienen und Milbenkontrolle brauchen schon während der aktiven Saison Aufmerksamkeit.'],
 ['Beobachtung im Winter','Beginnen Sie außen: Dach, Fluglochzugang, Standfestigkeit und Veränderungen nach Wind oder Schnee. Gewichtsangaben müssen zur Beutenkonstruktion passen. Eine Beobachtung beweist weder Gesundheit noch Verlust des Volkes.']
],[['Die Beute wirkt deutlich leichter','Dokumentieren Sie die Gewichtsschätzung. Vergleichen Sie frühere Aufzeichnungen und besprechen Sie Vorräte mit einer örtlichen Fachperson. Übernehmen Sie keine Futtermenge aus einem anderen Klima.'],['Eine innere Durchsicht ist nötig','Bestimmen Sie zuerst eine konkrete Frage. Wählen Sie geeignete Bedingungen und Methode; öffnen Sie das Nest nicht täglich für einen App-Eintrag.']],['Datum und Wetter','Methode der Vorratsbewertung','Äußere Veränderungen und Fotos','Klares Ziel der nächsten Kontrolle'],[['Muss ich die Beute täglich öffnen?','Nein. Eine tägliche Notiz kann eine äußere Beobachtung statt einer Nestdurchsicht beschreiben.'],['Bedeutet das Winterdesign, dass das Volk überwintern soll?','Nein. Das Design folgt Monat und Hemisphäre, Entscheidungen folgen örtlichen Bedingungen.']])}
});
